# What You're Doing, verse (figure 63.2)
# Eight bars; verses followed by another verse add a ninth bar, with a two-bar repeat of the
# ostinato over the last two (marked "-- ostinato ---"). Added: the ostinato's notes, from
# figure 63.1.
# Pollack labels the ninth bar's G "V", a slip for IV (the essay: V is held back until the end of
# the bridge); it is labelled IV here.
